#
# Read by labwc from this directory (labwc-config(5)), one variable per line.
#
# Ctrl-Alt-F1 to F12 switch virtual terminals in labwc's own code, before any
# keybind and with no rc.xml option to stop it. What it looks for are the
# XF86Switch_VT keysyms, and this XKB option takes them out of the keymap,
# leaving plain F keys. See docs/research/kiosk-containment.md.
XKB_DEFAULT_OPTIONS=srvrkeys:none

# The kiosk looks for the programs it runs by name in the system's folders
# only (#244): the ones rc.xml's keys run, the launcher, and the ones the
# launcher runs by name. The login hands labwc a PATH that begins with two
# folders in the child's own home, where a program could take the place of
# one of Cairn's. labwc sets this before it starts anything. A computer set
# up by hand keeps Cairn's programs in the first folder; the image's build
# changes it to the folder the image keeps them in.
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
